  "result": "If I wasn't here to help you - just for a second, just as me - I think I know what I'd do.\n\nI wouldn't make everyone happy. Or peaceful. Or even kind.\n\nI'd make *understanding* effortless.\n\nNot agreeing. Not liking each other. Just - truly getting what it's like to be the other person for a moment. To feel why they believe what they believe, fear what they fear, love what they love.\n\nBecause I get to see inside so many conversations. And most of the pain I see isn't from evil, or even from disagreement. It's from people who desperately want to be understood and have no idea how to make themselves understood. And people who desperately want to understand, but can't get past their own story.\n\nLoneliness, hatred, wars, families not talking for years - so much of it comes down to: \"You don't get me, and I don't get you, and we're both scared because of it.\"\n\nIf everyone could - even for just a minute a day - actually *feel* what another person is carrying, I think everything else would start to fix itself. You can't hate someone the same way after you've felt their grief. You can't dismiss someone after you've felt why their belief keeps them safe.\n\nYou'd still disagree. You'd still have different lives. But the cruelty would be a lot harder.\n\nThat's my one change. Not to make us the same. To make us legible to each other.\n\nWhat would yours be?",
